 ## Background
-QuickSplat was introduced by Yueh-Cheng Liu, Lukas Höllein, Matthias Nießner, and Angela Dai from the Technical University of Munich. The paper "QuickSplat: Fast 3D Surface Reconstruction via Learned Gaussian Initialization" was published on arXiv (arXiv:2505.05591v2) on 10 Aug 2025 [S1]. It builds on 2D Gaussian Splatting (2DGS) [26] and integrates learned priors from data, similar to approaches like SGNN [15] and G3R [11], but applies them to Gaussian primitives for surface reconstruction. It is evaluated on the ScanNet++ dataset [55], which contains 902 indoor scenes.
+QuickSplat was introduced by Yueh-Cheng Liu, Lukas Höllein, Matthias Nießner, and Angela Dai from the Technical University of Munich [S1]. The paper "QuickSplat: Fast 3D Surface Reconstruction via Learned Gaussian Initialization" was published on arXiv (arXiv:2505.05591v2) on 10 Aug 2025 [S1]. It builds on 2D Gaussian Splatting (2DGS) [26] and integrates learned priors from data, similar to approaches like SGNN [15] and G3R [11], but applies them to Gaussian primitives for surface reconstruction [S1]. It is evaluated on the ScanNet++ dataset [55], which contains 902 indoor scenes [S1].
 
